{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 64, :comments ["<b>And she saw Isaac.</b> She saw him majestic and was astonished because of him (Bereshit Rabbah)." "<b>And she fell.</b> She lowered herself toward the ground — as the Targum renders: וְאִתְרְכִינַת. She inclined herself toward the ground but did not reach the floor, as in ״הַטִּי נָא כַדֵּךְ״, אַרְכִינִי, and ״וַיֵּט שָׁמַיִם״ (Psalms 18) — and אַרְכִּן is a term of inclining toward the ground. Similar to it: ״כִּי יִפֹּל לֹא יוּטָל״ (Psalms 37) — that is, if he inclines toward the ground, he will not reach the floor."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:00:21.361137431Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}